IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-elector`
IMPORT `ea-qa`

-- Electoral Act 1907 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (ea-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and every
-- situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the two roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error. Each
-- question with a situation input is asked, for its own role, with the situation FALSE and every later input ASSUMEd.
-- For the elector (the baseline's seat), each question is also asked against the baseline export on the same facts:
-- the layer's answer must be the baseline's, wrapped in the layer's answer type. Expected values are worked by hand
-- from the deposited text, never copied from the output. The people are those of the baseline's cases (Chloe, born 14
-- March 2003; Jake, born 30 August 2006) and HYPOTHETICAL others, named as such.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked date` IS A DATE
ASSUME `unasked circumstances` IS AN `About me`
ASSUME `an unasked response` IS A `My response to the penalty notice`
ASSUME `an unasked offence` IS A `My offence`
ASSUME `an unasked way onto the roll` IS A `How I came onto the Commonwealth roll`
ASSUME `an unasked kind of election` IS A `Kind of election`

`as the elector` MEANS `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector`
`as the employer` MEANS `I employ someone who is a State elector`
`as the candidate` MEANS `I am a candidate, or want to stand, at a State election`

`a district election` MEANS `an election in a district, for the Legislative Assembly`
`a Council election` MEANS `a Council election, for the Legislative Council`

GIVEN `born` IS A DATE, `living there since` IS A DATE, `enrolment` IS A `My enrolment`
      `visa` IS A BOOLEAN, `in prison for a year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My circumstances`
`a citizen` MEANS `My circumstances` WITH
    `my date of birth` IS `born`
    `I am an Australian citizen` IS NOT `visa`
    `I am a British subject who was an elector within 3 months before 26 January 1984` IS FALSE
    `I hold a temporary visa or am an unlawful noncitizen` IS `visa`
    `I am the subject of a lack of capacity notice` IS FALSE
    `I am off the Commonwealth roll for this State on the ground in Commonwealth section 93(8)(a)` IS FALSE
    `I was convicted of treason and have not been pardoned` IS FALSE
    `I am serving or yet to serve detention or imprisonment of 1 year or longer` IS `in prison for a year`
    `I am under indefinite imprisonment, a Criminal Code order or supervision` IS FALSE
    `the day I began living in my district` IS `living there since`
    `my enrolment` IS `enrolment`

`Chloe` MEANS `a citizen` (Date 14 3 2003) (Date 14 3 2003) `enrolled for the district I live in` FALSE FALSE
`Jake` MEANS `a citizen` (Date 30 8 2006) (Date 30 8 2006) `not enrolled` FALSE FALSE
-- HYPOTHETICAL: an enrolled prisoner serving 2 years; a temporary visa holder; Mia, born 1 January 2008, unenrolled
-- and enrolled; Sam, who moved into his district on 1 February 2025.
`the prisoner` MEANS `a citizen` (Date 1 1 1990) (Date 1 1 2010) `enrolled for the district I live in` FALSE TRUE
`the visa holder` MEANS `a citizen` (Date 1 1 1990) (Date 1 1 2010) `not enrolled` TRUE FALSE
`Mia` MEANS `a citizen` (Date 1 1 2008) (Date 1 1 2008) `not enrolled` FALSE FALSE
`Mia enrolled` MEANS `a citizen` (Date 1 1 2008) (Date 1 1 2008) `enrolled for the district I live in` FALSE FALSE
`Sam` MEANS `a citizen` (Date 1 1 1990) (Date 1 2 2025) `enrolled for the district I live in` FALSE FALSE

-- The same people as the layer asks them (Q9 in NOTES.md): citizenship, the s 18(2) bars and the further s 18(1) bars are
-- one yes/no each. The equality cases ask the layer on these and the baseline on the records above, where the visa holder
-- is "not a citizen" and "holds a temporary visa" and the prisoner is "serving 1 year or longer", the first field of each
-- group.
GIVEN `born` IS A DATE, `living there since` IS A DATE, `enrolment` IS A `My enrolment`
      `visa` IS A BOOLEAN, `in prison for a year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `About me`
`a citizen, as asked` MEANS `About me` WITH
    `my date of birth` IS `born`
    `I am an Australian citizen, or a British subject who was an elector within 3 months before 26 January 1984` IS NOT `visa`
    `I am the subject of a lack of capacity notice, am off the Commonwealth roll for this State on the ground in Commonwealth section 93(8)(a), was convicted of treason and have not been pardoned, or hold a temporary visa or am an unlawful noncitizen` IS `visa`
    `I am serving or yet to serve detention or imprisonment of 1 year or longer, or am under indefinite imprisonment, a Criminal Code order or supervision` IS `in prison for a year`
    `the day I began living in my district` IS `living there since`
    `my enrolment` IS `enrolment`

`Chloe, as asked` MEANS `a citizen, as asked` (Date 14 3 2003) (Date 14 3 2003) `enrolled for the district I live in` FALSE FALSE
`Jake, as asked` MEANS `a citizen, as asked` (Date 30 8 2006) (Date 30 8 2006) `not enrolled` FALSE FALSE
`the prisoner, as asked` MEANS `a citizen, as asked` (Date 1 1 1990) (Date 1 1 2010) `enrolled for the district I live in` FALSE TRUE
`the visa holder, as asked` MEANS `a citizen, as asked` (Date 1 1 1990) (Date 1 1 2010) `not enrolled` TRUE FALSE
`Mia, as asked` MEANS `a citizen, as asked` (Date 1 1 2008) (Date 1 1 2008) `not enrolled` FALSE FALSE
`Mia enrolled, as asked` MEANS `a citizen, as asked` (Date 1 1 2008) (Date 1 1 2008) `enrolled for the district I live in` FALSE FALSE
`Sam, as asked` MEANS `a citizen, as asked` (Date 1 1 1990) (Date 1 2 2025) `enrolled for the district I live in` FALSE FALSE

GIVEN `voted` IS A BOOLEAN, `away` IS A BOOLEAN, `religious` IS A BOOLEAN, `satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What happened at the election`
`at the election` MEANS `What happened at the election` WITH
    `I voted` IS `voted`
    `I was outside the State, and that prevented me voting` IS `away`
    `I had a mental or physical impairment on the voting days` IS FALSE
    `I honestly believe abstaining from voting is part of my religious duty` IS `religious`
    `I had another valid and sufficient reason` IS FALSE
    `the Commissioner is satisfied of my absence, ineligibility or reason` IS `satisfied`

`did not vote, no reason` MEANS `at the election` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`voted at it` MEANS `at the election` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`away from the State, Commissioner satisfied` MEANS `at the election` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE
`did not vote, religious belief` MEANS `at the election` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

`8 March 2025` MEANS Date 8 3 2025

