-- Added after verification (6 November 2026; Q9 in NOTES.md): each group the layer asks as one yes/no, against the
-- baseline on a record that sets a field of the group other than the first. HYPOTHETICAL people.
GIVEN `british` IS A BOOLEAN, `treason` IS A BOOLEAN, `indefinite` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My circumstances`
`a non-citizen elector of 1983` MEANS `My circumstances` WITH
    `my date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
    `I am an Australian citizen` IS FALSE
    `I am a British subject who was an elector within 3 months before 26 January 1984` IS `british`
    `I hold a temporary visa or am an unlawful noncitizen` IS FALSE
    `I am the subject of a lack of capacity notice` IS FALSE
    `I am off the Commonwealth roll for this State on the ground in Commonwealth section 93(8)(a)` IS FALSE
    `I was convicted of treason and have not been pardoned` IS `treason`
    `I am serving or yet to serve detention or imprisonment of 1 year or longer` IS FALSE
    `I am under indefinite imprisonment, a Criminal Code order or supervision` IS `indefinite`
    `the day I began living in my district` IS Date 1 1 1980
    `my enrolment` IS `enrolled for the district I live in`

GIVEN `qualified` IS A BOOLEAN, `barred from enrolment` IS A BOOLEAN, `barred from voting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `About me`
`a non-citizen elector of 1983, as asked` MEANS `About me` WITH
    `my date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
    `I am an Australian citizen, or a British subject who was an elector within 3 months before 26 January 1984` IS `qualified`
    `I am the subject of a lack of capacity notice, am off the Commonwealth roll for this State on the ground in Commonwealth section 93(8)(a), was convicted of treason and have not been pardoned, or hold a temporary visa or am an unlawful noncitizen` IS `barred from enrolment`
    `I am serving or yet to serve detention or imprisonment of 1 year or longer, or am under indefinite imprisonment, a Criminal Code order or supervision` IS `barred from voting`
    `the day I began living in my district` IS Date 1 1 1980
    `my enrolment` IS `enrolled for the district I live in`

-- s 17(1)(a)(ii): a British subject who was an elector before 26 January 1984 is qualified, and may vote.
